      "kind": "BRUTE_FORCE",
      "language": "JAVASCRIPT",
      "title": "List the order and splice",
      "intuition": "With the order written out, the k-th from the back is just an index.",
      "approach": "Collect the chain order into an array and remove index length - k.",
      "pseudocode": "order = chain from head; remove order[len - k]; return order",
      "code": "function dropNthCar(next, head, k) {\n  const order = [];\n  for (let car = head; car !== -1; car = next[car]) order.push(car);\n  order.splice(order.length - k, 1);\n  return order;\n}",
      "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
      "spaceComplexity": "O(n)",
      "commonMistakes": [
        "Removing index k from the front instead of from the back."
      ],
      "interviewExplanation": "Copying the order into an array is simple and linear but needs O(n) extra space and doesn't exercise pointer manipulation.",
